WEBVTT

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:41.851
I'll grant you a handicap.

00:01:45.146 --> 00:01:50.151
After all, the price you'll pay playing
against us will be unfathomable.

00:01:55.198 --> 00:02:01.204
"Reflection and Illusion"

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.177
You've got skills, Egg.

00:02:16.177 --> 00:02:18.805
I'm hoping to become a doctor,
so I can handle this much.

00:02:19.681 --> 00:02:21.975
I'm just glad you're okay.

00:02:24.519 --> 00:02:28.398
W-Wait! You middle schoolers don't
stand a chance against them!

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:33.486
You need to learn Synchronization
before you take on those twins!

00:02:35.739 --> 00:02:37.949
We're great at that.

00:02:38.533 --> 00:02:40.744
Right, Eiji?

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:43.663
Of course!

00:02:45.331 --> 00:02:49.252
After all, we're Seigaku's Golden Pair!

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:09.773
Professor, I swear I'll make something

00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:14.027
of the potential you gave me.

00:03:19.949 --> 00:03:23.495
The middle schoolers in black jerseys
are putting up a good fight.

00:03:23.912 --> 00:03:24.621
Yes.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:25.955
Oh?

00:03:26.331 --> 00:03:30.669
An interesting game's about to
begin on this court, as well.

00:03:31.836 --> 00:03:37.092
You're the one who recommended
Yukimura-<i>kun </i>for selection, weren't you?

00:03:37.884 --> 00:03:41.638
Is there some reason you
chose one middle schooler?

00:03:50.814 --> 00:03:54.734
You must not think much of me.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:58.321
I can't believe a middle schooler
is challenging me to play.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.074
Let's just start the match.

00:04:18.883 --> 00:04:21.094
You know tennis better than I expected!

00:04:30.186 --> 00:04:33.606
But you're still only a middle schooler.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.775
You're not reading me well enough.

00:04:48.997 --> 00:04:50.874
It's an experience gap.

00:04:50.874 --> 00:04:54.377
The broad defensive range of
an all-rounder like yourself

00:04:54.377 --> 00:04:56.880
is sometimes a weakness.

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:03.386
You were too focused on returning
the ball to notice the change in its spin.

00:05:06.014 --> 00:05:08.350
Well? What will you do?

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:11.728
You've already revealed several weaknesses.

00:05:11.728 --> 00:05:15.398
You can find all the weaknesses you want.

00:05:15.732 --> 00:05:18.109
I'm just playing tennis my way.

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:21.404
Are you saying you'll give
me a head-to-head battle?

00:05:22.864 --> 00:05:24.324
Head-to-head?

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:32.123
Move like lightning!

00:05:49.808 --> 00:05:53.645
I will beat you in a head-to-head battle!

00:05:58.983 --> 00:06:00.568
You've returned...

00:06:02.821 --> 00:06:05.115
...as my powerful rival.

00:06:07.701 --> 00:06:09.202
You must be going soft!

00:06:10.662 --> 00:06:14.833
That's why I can't afford to drop
a single game from now on.

00:06:21.339 --> 00:06:25.802
I'm not pure enough for
head-to-head battles.

00:06:39.607 --> 00:06:42.152
Trying to outsmart me won't work.

00:06:47.032 --> 00:06:50.493
I've been looking forward to your return.

00:06:51.202 --> 00:06:54.414
How was training abroad?

00:06:55.165 --> 00:06:57.042
Meet any interesting players?

00:06:58.126 --> 00:07:00.670
Is playing in a foreign country a big hurdle?

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:03.423
Come on, tell me everything.

00:07:04.591 --> 00:07:07.427
Your tennis hasn't changed.

00:07:08.803 --> 00:07:11.348
When I think right, you go right.

00:07:11.723 --> 00:07:14.225
When I think left, you go left.

00:07:15.101 --> 00:07:18.563
Your style of reading your opponent's
emotions and striking first

00:07:18.563 --> 00:07:21.066
may have worked until now...

00:07:22.108 --> 00:07:22.901
But...

00:07:28.782 --> 00:07:32.035
Against me as I am now,
it's no more than a joke.

00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:40.043
Seriously?

00:07:40.043 --> 00:07:42.295
They're using Synchronization!

00:07:48.677 --> 00:07:49.302
Eiji!

00:07:49.678 --> 00:07:50.720
Got it!

00:07:51.221 --> 00:07:53.640
Australian Formation!

00:08:02.065 --> 00:08:02.649
Now!

00:08:03.066 --> 00:08:03.817
Yep!

00:08:06.194 --> 00:08:09.572
Kikumaru Bazooka!

00:08:12.534 --> 00:08:13.410
It's no use.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.412
Their Synchronization is too strong!

00:08:17.247 --> 00:08:18.164
Watch out!

00:08:24.254 --> 00:08:26.881
A-Are you okay, Niou?

00:08:29.009 --> 00:08:30.218
Ouch.

00:08:30.552 --> 00:08:33.555
That punch was a real stunner.

00:08:34.681 --> 00:08:39.477
In a Synchronization match,
the more skilled team wins.

00:08:41.688 --> 00:08:43.273
The Golden Pair, was it?

00:08:44.065 --> 00:08:45.817
You're not living up to your name.

00:08:49.362 --> 00:08:50.238
Don't.

00:08:51.156 --> 00:08:54.034
They'll turn you into a boiled egg.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.582
It's not easy to erase the memory of a loss.

00:09:00.915 --> 00:09:04.794
It sticks to you and eventually turns into fear.

00:09:06.379 --> 00:09:09.007
If you want to give up, now's the time.

00:09:11.926 --> 00:09:15.847
Or would you like another handicap?

00:09:17.182 --> 00:09:20.518
How long are you going to keep up this farce?

00:09:20.852 --> 00:09:21.936
What?

00:09:22.562 --> 00:09:26.149
Why not take off that blindfold?

00:09:28.610 --> 00:09:30.236
Fool!

00:09:30.236 --> 00:09:34.282
I'll make you regret negating my kindness!

00:09:43.667 --> 00:09:45.251
What's going on?

00:09:46.336 --> 00:09:47.295
I...

00:09:48.254 --> 00:09:49.631
...can't see!

00:10:05.647 --> 00:10:06.981
Would you like me

00:10:08.358 --> 00:10:10.360
to take your other senses, too?

00:10:12.821 --> 00:10:15.115
You take away people's senses?

00:10:17.367 --> 00:10:18.743
That's dangerous.

00:10:20.787 --> 00:10:24.374
You look rather triumphant,

00:10:24.958 --> 00:10:26.793
but you should be careful.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:36.803
My eyes are reflections.

00:10:38.013 --> 00:10:40.807
Everything you do reflects back to you.

00:10:58.408 --> 00:11:01.161
Let's end this, Irie.

00:11:03.621 --> 00:11:04.497
No!

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:08.209
I don't want it to end here!

00:11:09.252 --> 00:11:10.837
Accept it.

00:11:10.837 --> 00:11:13.381
Now that we've experienced the world,

00:11:13.381 --> 00:11:16.384
this is the difference
between your skill and ours.

00:11:17.218 --> 00:11:19.804
I refuse to accept that!

00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:21.473
I can't!

00:11:22.349 --> 00:11:24.476
You have great skill,

00:11:25.185 --> 00:11:27.228
yet you didn't turn your
attention to the world.

00:11:27.771 --> 00:11:29.773
That is why you lose.

00:11:30.732 --> 00:11:36.196
You'll regret staying here to raise
the standards of the Japanese team.

00:11:39.657 --> 00:11:41.826
I want to turn my attention to the world!

00:11:42.202 --> 00:11:44.120
No, I wanted to!

00:11:44.621 --> 00:11:50.335
But I know I'm not tall
enough to take on the world!

00:12:03.056 --> 00:12:04.432
Just kidding.

00:12:14.025 --> 00:12:19.239
You try too hard to dramatize
matches with your cheap acting.

00:12:19.989 --> 00:12:21.533
Give it a rest.

00:12:29.874 --> 00:12:30.959
Do you...

00:12:34.045 --> 00:12:36.673
...have any idea whose acting
you're criticizing?

00:12:50.812 --> 00:12:52.230
Atobe-<i>kun</i>.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.236
What's up?

00:12:58.236 --> 00:12:59.612
Getting out of the rain?

00:13:00.905 --> 00:13:02.240
Let me ask you something.

00:13:02.907 --> 00:13:06.995
What you said at the end of our match...

00:13:10.248 --> 00:13:14.461
Man, I'm impressed.

00:13:16.129 --> 00:13:19.883
I can't lift my shoulder anymore.

00:13:21.468 --> 00:13:22.886
Nice fight.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:29.768
Did you really mean that?

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:35.273
The answer is both yes and no.

00:13:38.443 --> 00:13:39.569
I see.

00:13:39.986 --> 00:13:41.363
You're not mad?

00:13:41.946 --> 00:13:46.451
I'm not tasteless enough to
criticize genuine acting.

00:13:52.457 --> 00:13:56.294
"We are such stuff
As dreams are made on..."

00:13:58.546 --> 00:14:00.090
That's Shakespeare.

00:14:02.258 --> 00:14:03.343
You recognize it?

00:14:04.427 --> 00:14:05.929
Of course.

00:14:06.513 --> 00:14:07.847
Everyone knows that.

00:14:10.350 --> 00:14:12.727
I don't care if this world

00:14:13.186 --> 00:14:18.441
is real or a dream,
or if tennis is acting or not.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:24.072
Miracles are born in the chaos of the court.

00:14:24.698 --> 00:14:28.243
I just want to observe that moment.

00:14:31.913 --> 00:14:33.206
I put on

00:14:33.623 --> 00:14:36.584
an earnest performance to
create a miracle in that match.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:40.505
I can see right through you!

00:14:40.505 --> 00:14:45.760
And I saw a miracle in your tennis.

00:14:45.760 --> 00:14:47.554
Atobe Kingdom.

00:14:47.887 --> 00:14:50.765
That may have been the first time

00:14:50.765 --> 00:14:53.184
my feelings had ever been so uplifted.

00:14:59.733 --> 00:15:04.946
I'll keep my promise, Tezuka!

00:15:09.409 --> 00:15:10.827
Just kidding.

00:15:14.122 --> 00:15:15.415
I'm borrowing this.

00:15:17.625 --> 00:15:19.919
I feel like reading it again.

00:15:20.337 --> 00:15:21.588
Go ahead.

00:15:34.559 --> 00:15:37.937
"We are such stuff
As dreams are made on..."

00:15:38.772 --> 00:15:40.315
Recognize that, Akiba-<i>kun</i>?

00:15:40.315 --> 00:15:42.734
Huh? What's that?

00:15:43.109 --> 00:15:44.277
I should've known.

00:15:44.277 --> 00:15:48.114
And to think you called my acting cheap.

00:15:48.114 --> 00:15:50.408
Makes me feel pretty pathetic.

00:15:56.873 --> 00:15:59.584
Maybe I was right not to go abroad.

00:15:59.959 --> 00:16:02.879
There are no signs of miracles
on the court today.

00:16:04.589 --> 00:16:07.133
It's time to lower the curtain.

00:16:17.227 --> 00:16:20.980
You're useless without Synchronization, Egg.

00:16:23.441 --> 00:16:27.862
You seem like you're out of tricks, too.

00:16:30.031 --> 00:16:32.492
Th-This is rough.

00:16:33.368 --> 00:16:35.370
As it is, they say that twins

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:40.375
perfectly understand each other's
thoughts and movements.

00:16:47.298 --> 00:16:48.591
That's it!

00:16:49.009 --> 00:16:49.759
Niou!

00:16:50.468 --> 00:16:53.179
I see. We can try that.

00:16:53.596 --> 00:16:57.726
It's do or die. Might be worth a shot.

00:17:00.478 --> 00:17:01.688
That's right.

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:07.736
We can't lose here.

00:17:11.031 --> 00:17:12.240
That's right.

00:17:12.240 --> 00:17:16.161
We have to complete our revolution.

00:17:17.287 --> 00:17:19.205
You guys never learn.

00:17:19.205 --> 00:17:22.208
No matter how long this match
goes on, you can't beat us.

00:17:25.170 --> 00:17:26.796
Are you sure about that?

00:17:27.339 --> 00:17:28.465
What?

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.842
Oishi Territory!

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.180
Impossible!

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:37.766
He's Synchronizing with us?

00:17:38.141 --> 00:17:42.062
I can see all your thoughts and movements...

00:17:42.645 --> 00:17:44.230
Through your triplet!

00:17:44.689 --> 00:17:45.482
Puri.

00:18:02.082 --> 00:18:05.418
These eyes are mirrors reflecting you.

00:18:05.418 --> 00:18:09.964
Every move you make against
me is reflected back to you.

00:18:13.426 --> 00:18:17.180
How long do you intend to keep playing blind?

00:18:17.514 --> 00:18:20.308
You've already lost this match!

00:18:27.273 --> 00:18:28.983
You brought this upon yourself.

00:18:31.611 --> 00:18:33.697
You really don't know when to give up.

00:18:34.906 --> 00:18:36.491
I can't give up.

00:18:37.117 --> 00:18:41.121
I can't lose here.

00:18:46.543 --> 00:18:47.544
Now...

00:18:48.712 --> 00:18:49.963
Let's continue.

00:18:51.715 --> 00:18:55.927
You'll soon know exactly
what kind of consequences

00:18:56.803 --> 00:18:59.180
your reckless challenge will bring.

00:19:17.991 --> 00:19:20.452
Looks like your sense of hearing is gone, too.

00:19:46.102 --> 00:19:49.230
I didn't feel myself hitting the ball.

00:19:52.901 --> 00:19:53.860
My body...

00:19:54.652 --> 00:19:57.238
And now you've lost your sense of touch.

00:20:00.492 --> 00:20:03.119
I feel weak...

00:20:09.501 --> 00:20:12.420
After experiencing the pain
inflicted by your own ability,

00:20:12.879 --> 00:20:16.466
you will never be able to
take another's senses again.

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:20.428
This is the cost of your reckless challenge.

00:20:20.845 --> 00:20:23.640
Goodbye, strong middle schooler.

00:20:39.739 --> 00:20:41.366
That image

00:20:41.366 --> 00:20:45.078
is merely an illusion created by your mind.

00:20:46.246 --> 00:20:50.458
Enjoy the rest of your dream by yourself.

00:20:55.839 --> 00:21:00.093
Looks like he didn't
betray your expectations.

00:21:01.344 --> 00:21:03.221
He exceeded my expectations.

00:21:06.224 --> 00:21:08.101
Seiichi Yukimura...

00:21:09.102 --> 00:21:10.478
Interesting.

00:21:29.539 --> 00:21:31.875
I'm taking this, Akiba-<i>kun</i>.

00:21:32.334 --> 00:21:34.044
Thanks to you,

00:21:34.044 --> 00:21:35.920
I've broadened the scope of my acting.

00:21:39.215 --> 00:21:41.968
This is becoming quite interesting.

00:21:44.846 --> 00:21:45.805
Let's go.

00:23:18.398 --> 00:23:19.399
"Next Time"

00:23:19.399 --> 00:23:21.901
"Next Time"
Now that the U-17 first string has returned,

00:23:21.901 --> 00:23:22.444
Now that the U-17 first string has returned,

00:23:22.444 --> 00:23:25.280
the training camp's getting really exciting.

00:23:25.280 --> 00:23:28.450
Shuffle matches for a spot on
the Japanese team sound fun.

00:23:28.450 --> 00:23:31.786
I won't lose, no matter who I face.

00:23:33.705 --> 00:23:35.790
You've grown quite bold.

00:23:35.790 --> 00:23:37.959
But you're still not strong enough.

00:23:37.959 --> 00:23:39.419
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:23:39.836 --> 00:23:41.880
Wait, who are you?

00:23:41.880 --> 00:23:45.550
"The Night Before the Battle"
The next episode of <i>New Prince of Tennis</i>
is: "The Night Before the Battle."

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:48.480
"The Night Before the Battle"
It's been a while, shorty.
